From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrmikedrum <mrmikedrum@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:58:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Show every mode when a charm is described before it has an
 activator

CharmEffect filters modes by legal targets, which needs an activating player. Rendering a modal
trigger's text before anyone activates it reached that filter with none and failed. Without an
activator, describe all modes; choosing modes is unchanged.

Goldfish-Upstream: offer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/CharmEffect.java | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/CharmEffect.java b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/CharmEffect.java
index 92517d0d..eaf95a3f 100644
--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/CharmEffect.java
+++ b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/effects/CharmEffect.java
@@ -36,7 +36,9 @@ public class CharmEffect extends SpellAbilityEffect {
 
         List<AbilitySub> choices = Lists.newArrayList(sa.getAdditionalAbilityList("Choices"));
 
-        if (source.getZone() != null) {
+        // Card text is also rendered before an ability has an activating player.
+        // In that case show all modes, rather than querying legal targets.
+        if (source.getZone() != null && sa.getActivatingPlayer() != null) {
             List<AbilitySub> toRemove = Lists.newArrayList();
             for (AbilitySub ch : choices) {
                 // 603.3c If one of the modes would be illegal, that mode can't be chosen.
